course: dictionary
lesson: 2585
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Context, the words and sentences around the word, tells you which meaning the writer chose. Look for clues before you decide.
explain: «Christians belong to different families of churches called denominations.» Here the clues are Christians and churches, so denomination means one of the separate groups within a religion, such as Catholic, Anglican, Methodist or Baptist.
explain: «A five-pound note and a ten-pound note are different denominations.» Here the clues are note and pound, so denomination means the value printed on a coin or banknote. Always check: does my meaning still make sense in the sentence?
fact: Denomination means one of the separate groups or branches of a religion, such as Catholic, Anglican, Methodist or Baptist.
fact: Christian denominations share the same core beliefs about Jesus but have different traditions and ways of worshipping.
fact: Denomination also means the value printed on a coin or banknote, as in «notes in small denominations».
fact: «Non-denominational» churches are independent churches that are not part of a larger denomination.
exercise: «Christians belong to different families of churches called denominations.» What is a denomination here? | A Bible verse read aloud | A tall church tower | *A group or branch of churches within a religion | A coin with a value printed on it
exercise: «A five-pound note and a ten-pound note are different denominations.» What does denomination mean in this sentence? | *The value printed on a note | A church service at the weekend | A kind of prayer | The name of a school subject
exercise: Which of these is a Christian denomination? | Heartbroken | Five-pound note | Mid | *Anglican
test: In «notes in small denominations», what does denomination mean? | A school subject | A kind of prayer | A group of churches | *The value printed on each note
test: Which statement about non-denominational churches is true? | They are part of one large denomination | *They are independent and not part of a larger denomination | They only meet in the summer | They are the same as Catholic churches
exam: Sophie says denomination always means a coin. Is she right? | Yes, and it also means a church building | Yes, it always means a coin | No, it always means a banknote | *No, it can also mean a group of churches within a religion
